# The C fixtures the kernel's generic rung runs: each /mnt/tests/<name>.elf,
# expected to exit 42 (requests/d-a-one-rung-for-every-c-fixture.md).
# scripts/create-ext4-rootfs.sh stages this file at /tests/ctest-generic.list
# and refuses it if a line is malformed or names a fixture with no
# services/<name>/build.py.
#
# One fixture a line, three fields separated by blanks:
#
#   name      the fixture, services/<name>/: its ELF, and its argv[0]
#   grants    "-" for none, or a comma-separated list of the words the
#             kernel's rung knows (`ctest_generic_grant`, kernel/src/proc/
#             spawn.rs, which the rootfs script reads), each at most once:
#             `file` is one wildcard File capability (READ | WRITE |
#             EXECUTE | METADATA)
#   seconds   how long it may take, from spawn to exit: 1 to 600
#
# and a fourth, for a fixture that runs a port only some worktrees build:
#
#   needs=<path>  what it runs, relative to the image's root: an image built
#             without it leaves the fixture off the staged list, with a
#             warning, rather than run it to fail every boot made from that
#             worktree (Opus's review of lane D's round 202)
#
# A fixture goes on only after it has passed in a lane D boot: none of
# another lane's boots should meet one of these failing for the first time.
#
# Lines commented out with "failed its first run" failed the 2026-10-21 boot,
# the first that ran this list; each comes back once it passes in a lane D
# boot (known-issues/D-SIXTEEN-C-FIXTURES-FAIL-THEIR-FIRST-RUN-ON-THE-GENERIC-RUNG.md).
#
# name           grants   seconds
ctest-obstack    -        30
ctest-argp       file     120
ctest-aio        file     30
ctest-cxx-throw  -        30
# ctest-eintr      -        120  (failed its first run -- timed out in a futex wait)
ctest-fortify-abort -        60
ctest-printf-streams -        30
ctest-pthread    -        120
ctest-stdio      file     60
ctest-sysvipc    -        30
ctest-ucontext   -        30
# ctest-llvm-tools file     600  needs=bin/llc  (failed its first run -- 51: ld.lld -static ... -lc returned 262)
ctest-sigpipe    -        30
ctest-rusage     -        60
# ctest-pi-mutex   -        60  (failed its first run -- 52: the low thread ran on ahead)
# ctest-system     file     60  (failed its first run -- 9: no /bin/sh while the battery sees the image at /mnt)
ctest-mmap-file  file     30
# Waiting on lane A's `creds` grant word -- (Process, SET_CREDENTIALS), to
# set their own ids -- which the rung does not know yet, and a word it does
# not know stops the whole list
# (requests/d-a-the-generic-rung-needs-the-creds-grant-word.md):
# ctest-resuid     creds    30
# ctest-groups     file,creds 30
ctest-fallocate  file     30
ctest-string     -        60
ctest-gdb-runs   file     300  needs=bin/gnu-gdb
# ctest-mono-runs  file     300  needs=lib/mono/checks/checks.exe  (failed its first run -- 12: a probe died on a signal)
# ctest-binutils-runs file     300  needs=bin/as  (failed its first run -- 73: size counts the .note.gnu.property as writes)
ctest-gcc-runs   file     600  needs=usr/bin/gcc
ctest-unix-socket file     60
ctest-shared-anon -        30
ctest-cloexec-exec file     30
ctest-record-locks file     30
ctest-fsetfl-append file     60
ctest-positional-io file     60
ctest-timed-join -        30
ctest-sigign-exec file     30
# ctest-renice     -        30  (failed its first run -- 23: reading pid 1's nice, ESRCH)
ctest-affinity   -        30
# ctest-siginfo    -        30  (failed its first run -- 61: one record of the child's three, then EINTR)
# ctest-tmpfile    file     30  (failed its first run -- 2: mkdir /tmp/ctest-tmpfile, EACCES)
# ctest-seals      file     30  (failed its first run -- 2: memfd_create(MFD_ALLOW_SEALING), ENOENT)
ctest-cpu-clocks -        60
# ctest-itimers    -        60  (failed its first run -- 11)
ctest-posix-timers -      60
# ctest-dumpable   file     30  (failed its first run -- 39)
# ctest-thread-masks -        30  (failed its first run -- 30)
ctest-sigev-thread -        30
# ctest-fifo       file     30  (failed its first run -- 9)
# ctest-setids     creds    30  (waiting on `creds`, as ctest-resuid above)
ctest-spawn-attrs file     30
# ctest-swap       file,creds 30  (waiting on `creds`, as ctest-resuid above)
ctest-scm-rights file     30
ctest-uts-namespace file     30
ctest-secureboot file,secureboot 30
ctest-signal-deaths -        30
# ctest-terminfo   file     60  (failed its first run -- 10)
